    "text": "Infinite inboxes, including prefixes where you don&#x27;t have to create inboxes before you use them -- they self create when you add a suffix.<p>Three types of inboxes:\n- One sender. Locks to the first domain to send email (except gmail, outlook, etc where it locks to an email account for obivous reasons. It bounces everyone else.\n- Temporary. Lasts for a while (24h, 7days, etc) then bounces. Received messages stay or go as per your choice.\n- Prefix. The most powerful. Declare a prefix like &quot;service&quot; and then invent any suffix, like &quot;service-netflix&quot; or &quot;service$bank&quot; and it creates a new one-sender inbox locked to whoever wrote first.<p>Bring you own domain. Bring your own AI (MCP server ready). Forwarding.<p>Please help me test it.",
